    <string name="help_hint">▲▼ to scroll    Back to return</string>
    <string name="help1_t">Getting started</string>
    <string name="help1_b">Lumen is a player: it contains no channels or content. On the sign-in page enter the server address of your IPTV provider (Xtream Codes), your username and your password. All three are provided by your provider.</string>
    <string name="help2_t">Navigation</string>
    <string name="help2_b">Use the arrow keys of the remote to move, OK to select and Back to go back. The tabs at the top are: For you, Live TV, Movies, Series, TV Guide and Settings. In lists, ⏪/⏩ or channel up/down jump by pages.</string>
    <string name="help3_t">Watching live TV</string>
    <string name="help3_b">While watching: ▲▼ change channel, ◀ opens the channel list, ▶ the program guide, Menu opens options (audio track, subtitles, sleep timer). Type a channel number with the 0-9 keys. The rewind key returns to the previous channel.</string>
    <string name="help4_t">Favorites and continue watching</string>
    <string name="help4_b">Long-press OK (or press Menu) on a channel, movie or series to add or remove it from Favorites. Movies and episodes remember where you stopped and appear in \"Continue watching\" on the For you tab.</string>
    <string name="help5_t">TV guide</string>
    <string name="help5_b">The program guide comes from your provider. If a channel has no guide, Lumen can look for it in a public guide by matching the channel name. You can switch this fallback on or off in Settings.</string>
    <string name="help6_t">Profiles</string>
    <string name="help6_b">There are 4 profiles. Each one keeps its own favorites, recent channels and resume points. Change profile from Settings.</string>
    <string name="help7_t">Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="help7_b">If sign-in fails, check the server address (including http:// and the port), username and password. If channels do not play, check your connection and your subscription. \"Too many connections\" means the account is already in use on other devices. Use \"Refresh lists and TV guide\" in Settings to reload everything.</string>
